  "answer": "The emails regarding Q2 budget revisions highlight several key adjustments and impacts. Karen Smith (CFO) announced revisions to the Q2 budget, shifting funds toward emerging market bonds and revising the profit forecast to $9.378 million, a 3.5% increase from previous estimates. However, Oliver Grant (Project Manager) reported that capital expenditure projects, including a new office building and IT infrastructure upgrade, came in 10% over budget, necessitating adjustments to financial projections. Additionally, Emily Rogers (Operations Manager) requested urgent approval for an unplanned $50,000 IT security expenditure, which will also affect the Q2 budget. Diana Wells (Chief Auditor) noted that these recent budget revisions are a focus for the upcoming Q2 audit, requiring accurate records to be available."
